Next, let us sketch the proof of (4.67). Consider the case where \(\kappa\) is a quadrilateral. Take \(\mathbf{v}\) in \(H^{1}(\kappa)^{2}\), \(\hat{\mathbf{v}}=\mathscr{F}_{\kappa}^{-1}\mathbf{v}\) and let us split \(\hat{\mathbf{v}}\) as follows:

(4.70) \[\hat{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{grad}\,\hat{q}+\mathbf{curl}\,\hat{\mathbf{\phi}}\]

where \(\hat{q}\) is the solution of

\[\mathcal{A}\hat{q}=\operatorname{div}\hat{\mathbf{v}}\quad\text{in }\hat{ \kappa},\quad\hat{q}|_{\hat{\infty}\hat{\kappa}}=0.\]

Since \(\hat{\kappa}\) is convex, Theorem I.1.8 says that \(\hat{q}\!\in\!H^{2}(\hat{\kappa})\) with

\[\|\hat{q}\|_{2,\hat{\kappa}}\leqslant C_{1}\,\|\operatorname{div}\hat{ \mathbf{v}}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}.\]

As a consequence we can find \(\hat{\phi}\) in \(H^{2}(\hat{\kappa})\) that satisfies (4.70) and

\[\|\hat{\sigma}^{2}\hat{\phi}/\partial\hat{x}_{1}^{2}\|_{0,\hat{ \kappa}}^{2}+\|\hat{\sigma}^{2}\hat{\phi}/\partial\hat{x}_{2}^{2}\|_{0,\hat{ \kappa}}^{2}\] \[\quad\leqslant C_{2}\{\|\partial\hat{v}_{1}/\partial\hat{x}_{2} \|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}+\|\partial\hat{v}_{2}/\partial\hat{x}_{1}\|_{0,\hat{ \kappa}}^{2}+\|\operatorname{div}\hat{\mathbf{v}}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}\}.\]

Thus a straightforward application of Theorem A.3 yields:

(4.71) \[|\hat{\pi}\hat{\mathbf{v}}-\hat{\mathbf{v}}|_{1,\hat{\kappa}}\leqslant C_{3}\{ \|\partial\hat{v}_{1}/\partial\hat{x}_{2}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}+\|\partial \hat{v}_{2}/\partial\hat{x}_{1}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}+\|\operatorname{div} \hat{\mathbf{v}}\|_{0,\hat{\kappa}}^{2}\}^{1/2},\]

and a similar upper bound (with a different constant) for \(\|\hat{\pi}\hat{\mathbf{v}}-\hat{\mathbf{v}}\|_{0,s,\hat{\kappa}}\). In view of (4.63) and the regularity of \(\mathscr{T}_{h}\), a simple calculation now leads to (4.67). 

Theorem 4.4 gives us the following inf-sup condition:

_for each \(q_{h}\!\in\!Q_{h}\), there exists \(\mathbf{v}_{h}\!\in\!D_{0h}\) such that_

\[(q_{h},\operatorname{div}\mathbf{v}_{h})=\|q_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}^{2},\]

_and_

\[\left\{\sum\limits_{\kappa\,\in\,\mathscr{T}_{h}}|\mathbf{v}_{h}|_{1,\kappa}^ {2}\right\}^{1/2}+\|\mathbf{v}_{h}\|_{0,s,\Omega}+\|\operatorname{div}\mathbf{ v}_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\leqslant C(s)\|q_{h}\|_{0,\Omega}\quad\quad\forall s\geqslant 2.\]

With the spaces \(D_{0h}\) and \(Q_{h}\) we propose the following discretization of Problem (4.8):

_Find a function \(p_{h}\) in \(Q_{h}\) satisfying_

(4.72) \[\begin{split}\int_{\Omega}p_{h}\operatorname{div}\mathbf{v}_{h} dx=&-\!\int_{\Omega}\mathbf{f}\!\cdot\!\mathbf{v}_{h}\,dx\\ &+\nu\sum\limits_{\kappa\,\in\,\mathscr{T}_{h}}\left\{\int_{ \kappa}(\dot{\iota}_{h})_{ij}(\partial v_{ni}/\partial x_{j})\,dx-\int_{\partial \kappa}M_{nt}(\dot{\iota}_{h})\mathbf{v}_{h}\!\cdot\!\mathbf{t}\,ds\right\}\\ &\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad \quad\quad\